// Mission TT4_1, OpenTT's own map: generated.
// Lunar Lobe (tt4_1): OpenTT's own Moon map (a 432 m mission area, gravity 0.45).
// Layout (x east, y north; green spawns south, blue north):
// (0, 0)       the Lobe: a crater (r 72 m, floor 11 m under the plain, rim 6 m up), an ice
// lake on its floor (looks only: no friction change) and in its middle the
// crash site: an old probe's engine, fuel tank, nose, spheres and pipes, half
// buried and tilted, a debris field and its skid furrow from the north-west;
// the reload arch east of the wreck; its rim breached north-north-east and
// south-south-west, boost pads in the breaches shoot into it, jump pads on
// its floor out;
// the rille    a winding channel (16 m floor, 8 to 11 m deep) from the west edge to the
// east edge, under the Lobe's rim and across its floor south of the wreck;
// rock saddles cross it at x -142 and 150;
// (124, 112), (-128, -104), (-118, 116), (132, -112)  smaller craters (r 28..38),
// a power-up on each floor, ice in the north-western one;
// small craters (r 9..28) all over the mare plain, boulder fields on the rims;
// health north and south;
// (120, 40)    a lunar base: a lander on its landing pad, a domed module, radar dishes
// and solar panels; a few more dishes and panels out on the plain.
// See tt_assets::data::mission.
